infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Interceptor order decides whether p99 tells the truth
  desc Global interceptors unwind in reverse — does metrics wrap the timeout, or sit inside it?
  compares
    - label Metrics OUTSIDE the timeout — p99 honest
      children
        - label Brackets the whole request
          desc Metrics is first-in, last-out, so its timer also wraps the timeout path
        - label Timed-out requests still counted
          desc catchError sees the slow request and records its real served duration
        - label p99 reflects served latency
          desc The dashboard number matches what clients actually experienced
    - label Metrics INSIDE the timeout — p99 lies
      children
        - label Timeout errors the stream first
          desc The 5s timeout fires before metrics' tap or catchError can run
        - label Tail latency under-counted
          desc The timer stops early, so the slow request never lands in the histogram
        - label p99 under-reports the truth
          desc Dashboards hide the requests that actually timed out
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
